WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.272
A collection plan translates the requirement into source priorities and lawful search activities.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:10.381
Break the main question into smaller information needs.

00:00:10.381 --> 00:00:18.384
For each need, identify likely source categories, expected evidence, collection order, time budget, and a clear owner.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:22.493
Prioritize sources by relevance, reliability, access, and cost.

00:00:22.493 --> 00:00:27.900
Official records or direct technical documentation may answer some questions efficiently.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:36.335
News, social sources, forums, imagery, maps, and archives may provide leads or context but often require more validation.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:40.444
Develop search concepts rather than one rigid query.

00:00:40.444 --> 00:00:47.581
Record key names, dates, products, locations, and public identifiers that are necessary to the requirement.

00:00:47.581 --> 00:00:52.123
Plan how terms may vary across languages or time.

00:00:52.123 --> 00:00:58.395
Search strategy should remain transparent and reproducible rather than relying on unexplained intuition.

00:00:58.395 --> 00:01:02.505
Build legal and ethical constraints into the plan.

00:01:02.505 --> 00:01:08.777
Document approved public access, organizational policy, privacy boundaries, handling requirements, and escalation points.

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:18.509
Do not plan to bypass access controls, use deceptive identities, obtain stolen credentials, or enter spaces that are not legitimately available.

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:20.023
Avoid overcollection.

00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:26.295
More data can increase false associations, privacy exposure, storage burden, and analytical noise.

00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:30.837
Collect the minimum material needed to evaluate the requirement.

00:01:30.837 --> 00:01:37.542
Sensitive personal information should not be gathered merely because it appears in a result.

00:01:37.542 --> 00:01:39.056
Include contingencies.

00:01:39.056 --> 00:01:44.463
A source may disappear, conflict with another record, or prove unreliable.

00:01:44.463 --> 00:01:50.735
Identify alternatives and specify when to pause for legal, privacy, or supervisory review.

00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:58.304
A good collection plan focuses effort while leaving room to adapt when evidence changes the direction.
